{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 52daf588. This replaces items 5 and 6 of ruling\n3316caa5. The condition is equal answers, so the fixture holds\nanswers and no inputs.\n\n1. Input. Record no input hash and wrap no reader. Position is the\n   identity of a call: the list, the owner, the case and the call\n   index. The histories are fixed, so the same position is the same\n   call. Pass each original object to the judge unchanged. The\n   capture wraps only the two exports of `judge.ts`.\n2. Answer. Encode each answer with a small tagged encoder that\n   keeps Map and Set entries in order and keeps optional fields\n   absent. Hash those bytes.\n3. Case labels. Yes: for a judgment made while a suite collects,\n   use the owning suite, a collection marker and the local index.\n   Move no setup and drop no call.\n4. Committed fixture. One row for each case: the list, the owner,\n   the case label, the call count, and the SHA-256 over the answer\n   hashes of that case in call order. This keeps the file small\n   with every call covered. Report its real size in the E1 note.\n5. Raw capture. Keep each answer's bytes and hash outside the\n   checkout, under `~/play/artroom-evidence/`. Cite the path and\n   the SHA-256 of the capture in the note.\n6. The test after the split passes on the committed rows alone. On\n   a difference it prints the case, both counts and each current\n   answer of that case. If the raw capture is present, it also\n   prints the first call index that differs and the baseline\n   answer. If the capture is absent, it prints the command that\n   makes it again at 270dc8c7.\n7. A changed call count in a case is a failure. Do not realign.\n\nThe owner boundary of 3316caa5 stands, with your correction: the\nLedger is `packages/derive/test/fixtures.ts`.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}